  "tableSteps": [
    "Use an open table about 3 feet across. The two edges 4 feet apart are the home edges: Side A, the Highlanders, on one, Side B, the Jade Falcons, on the other. Measure in inches.",
    "Terrain: each player takes three trees, three small buildings and three large buildings from the box. Side B places first; then take turns placing two pieces at a time, each within 24 inches of the centre. Trees within 4 inches of another tree, whoever placed them, form a patch of woods.",
    "The box’s small buildings are Medium (CF 4) and the large ones Heavy (CF 12). The app tracks each one’s CF under Scenario rules. The diagram shows one way to lay out the city.",
    "Before play, each side secretly buys 5 points of Battlefield Support in the app (Scenario rules), handing the phone over so the other side doesn’t see. Side A also picks its two Combat Intuition ’Mechs (not the Atlas).",
    "Deploy: Side B places one ’Mech at least 24 inches from the centre toward its home edge; on a 4-foot table that is right at the edge. Then Side A places two the same way. Repeat until all thirteen are down."
  ],
  "winningSummary": "Cripple or destroy every enemy ’Mech first. A ’Mech that leaves the table counts as destroyed. The book has no turn limit; the app stops at 12 turns, and then the side with more Structure left wins.",
